#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
The Eyes fit, tilting to the horizon explained, and Cerulean as points.

- EYES_FIT takes the Commander's measured numbers (zoom 0.8, lon -108,
  lat 66) and gains a turn (bearing), for Earth's axis leaning sideways in
  Eyes. In #fit mode the [ and ] keys turn the globe; Shift makes every key
  finer. The printed line now includes the turn.
- Small notes to the right of the 3D terrain tick box say how to tilt, turn
  and roll with a mouse or a trackpad, on Mac and Windows.
- Oil slicks and slick sources: every record drawn as a point at the wide
  zooms, from files made by pipeline/cerulean/harvest_points.py (added by
  this patch). Until those files exist the layers behave as before.

Needs patch_list_0917.py, patch_world_terrain.py and patch_boxes_ct.py first.
Run from the repo root:  python3 patch_eyes_cerulean.py
"""
